---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SupportBadge from '../components/SupportBadge.astro';
import KovirBand from '../components/KovirBand.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="Why Kovir Labs exists, how the kovir.org team decides what it builds, and how to reach us.">
  <section class="section container prose-page">
    <h1>About Kovir Labs</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Kovir Labs is the development arm of Kovir LLC. We build open software that supports mission-driven
      work at a meta scale: tools that many organizations can use, rather than custom builds for one.
    </p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
      Kovir LLC works alongside under-resourced, mission-driven organizations: nonprofits, aging-services
      agencies, and the people who run them. Again and again, those organizations hit the same problems,
      and the software that solves them is expensive, locked-in, or missing. Kovir Labs builds the missing
      pieces once, in the open, so every organization can use them.
    </p>

    <h2>Who decides what we build</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>What Kovir Labs officially supports is decided by the kovir.org team.</strong> Anyone can
      suggest an idea on the <a href="/ideas">community forum</a> or through the <a href="/contact?type=idea">contact form</a>.
      The team reviews ideas regularly and favors needs that many organizations share. Decisions are
      posted on the forum, so you can always see what was accepted, what's in progress, and what shipped.
    </p>
    <p>Every project carries one of three support levels:</p>
    <dl class="levels">
      <div class="card">
        <dt><SupportBadge support="official" /></dt>
        <dd>The kovir.org team has adopted this project. Kovir Labs supports and maintains it.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <dt><SupportBadge support="incubating" /></dt>
        <dd>Being evaluated by the kovir.org team. Useful today, but there's no support promise yet.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <dt><SupportBadge support="lab" /></dt>
        <dd>An experiment or side project. Use it, enjoy it, and expect rough edges.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <h2>Who builds it</h2>
    <p>
      Kovir Labs is run by Evan Gress. Everything is open source, usually under the Apache-2.0 license,
      and lives on <a href="https://github.com/kovirlabs">GitHub</a>. We prefer plain files, local-first
      tools and no lock-in, so an organization can always walk away with its data.
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Email <a href="mailto:info@kovir.org">info@kovir.org</a>.</li>
      <li>Post an idea or a question on the <a href="https://github.com/kovirlabs/community/discussions">community forum</a>.</li>
      <li>Use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>, which needs no GitHub account.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <KovirBand />
</Base>

<style>
  .prose-page { max-width: 48rem; }
  .prose-page h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; }
  .levels { display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; margin: 1rem 0 0; }
  .levels .card { display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; }
  .levels dd { margin: 0; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
</style>
